{"root_text": {"uid": "snp2.4", "lang": "en", "is_root": false, "title": "Blessings", "author": "Dr. R.L. Soni", "author_short": "Soni", "author_uid": "soni", "next": {"author_uid": "mills", "lang": "en", "name": "Spiky the Native Spirit ", "uid": "snp2.5"}, "previous": {"author_uid": "mills", "lang": "en", "name": "Conscience ", "uid": "snp2.3"}, "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset='UTF-8'>\n<meta name='author' content='Dr. R.L. Soni'>\n<title></title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<article id='snp2.4' lang='en'>\n<header>\n<h1 class='sutta'>2.4. Blessings</h1>\n</header>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc1' href='#sc1'>SC 1</a><span class='evam'>Thus have I heard</span>:</p>\n<p>Once while the Blessed One was staying in the vicinity of Sāvatthi, in the Jeta Grove, in Anāthapiṇḍika's monastery, a certain deity, whose surpassing brilliance and beauty illumined the entire Jeta Grove, late one night came to the presence of the Blessed One; having come to him and offered profound salutations he stood on one side and spoke to him reverently in the following verse:</p>\n<blockquote class='gatha'>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc2' href='#sc2'>SC 2</a>Many deities and human beings<br>\nHave pondered what are blessings,<br>\nWhich they hope will bring them safety:<br>\nDeclare to them, Sir, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><span class='add'>To this the Blessed One replied:</span></p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc3' href='#sc3'>SC 3</a>With fools no company keeping.<br>\nWith the wise ever consorting,<br>\nTo the worthy homage paying:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc4' href='#sc4'>SC 4</a>Congenial place to dwell,<br>\nIn the past merits making,<br>\nOne's self directed well:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc5' href='#sc5'>SC 5</a>Ample learning, in crafts ability,<br>\nWith a well-trained disciplining,<br>\nWell-spoken words, civility:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc6' href='#sc6'>SC 6</a>Mother, father well supporting,<br>\nWife and children duly cherishing,<br>\nTypes of work unconflicting:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc7' href='#sc7'>SC 7</a>Acts of giving, righteous living,<br>\nRelatives and kin supporting,<br>\nActions blameless then pursuing:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc8' href='#sc8'>SC 8</a>Avoiding evil and abstaining,<br>\nFrom besotting drinks refraining,<br>\nDiligence in Dhamma doing:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc9' href='#sc9'>SC 9</a>Right reverence and humility<br>\nContentment and a grateful bearing,<br>\nHearing Dhamma when it's timely:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc10' href='#sc10'>SC 10</a>Patience, meekness when corrected,<br>\nSeeing monks and then discussing<br>\nAbout the Dhamma when it's timely:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc11' href='#sc11'>SC 11</a>Self-restraint and holy life,<br>\nAll the Noble Truths in-seeing,<br>\nRealization of Nibbaana:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc12' href='#sc12'>SC 12</a>Though touched by worldly circumstances,<br>\nNever his mind is wavering,<br>\nSorrowless, stainless and secure:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc13' href='#sc13'>SC 13</a>Since by acting in this way,<br>\nThey are everywhere unvanquished,<br>\nAnd everywhere they go in safety:<br>\nTheirs, the Highest Blessings.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<footer>\n<p>Translated by <span class='author'>Dr. R.L. Soni</span>.</p>\n<p>From <cite class='book' translate='no'>Life's Highest Blessings: The Maha Mangala Sutta</cite>, translated by Dr. R.L. Soni (Kandy: Buddhist Publication Society, <span class='publication-date'>1987</span></p>\n<p>This text was sourced from <a href='https://accesstoinsight.org/'>Access to Insight</a>. The original contained the following notice.</p>\n<p><strong>Terms of use:</strong> You may copy, reformat, reprint, republish, and redistribute this work in any medium whatsoever, provided that: (1) you only make such copies, etc. available free of charge and, in the case of reprinting, only in quantities of no more than 50 copies; (2) you clearly indicate that any derivatives of this work (including translations) are derived from this source document; and (3) you include the full text of this license in any copies or derivatives of this work. Otherwise, all rights reserved.</p>\n<p>Prepared for SuttaCentral by a volunteer.</p>\n</footer>\n</article>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}, "translation": {"uid": "snp2.4", "lang": "en", "is_root": false, "title": "Blessings", "author": "Dr. R.L. Soni", "author_short": "Soni", "author_uid": "soni", "next": {"author_uid": "mills", "lang": "en", "name": "Spiky the Native Spirit ", "uid": "snp2.5"}, "previous": {"author_uid": "mills", "lang": "en", "name": "Conscience ", "uid": "snp2.3"}, "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset='UTF-8'>\n<meta name='author' content='Dr. R.L. Soni'>\n<title></title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<article id='snp2.4' lang='en'>\n<header>\n<h1 class='sutta'>2.4. Blessings</h1>\n</header>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc1' href='#sc1'>SC 1</a><span class='evam'>Thus have I heard</span>:</p>\n<p>Once while the Blessed One was staying in the vicinity of Sāvatthi, in the Jeta Grove, in Anāthapiṇḍika's monastery, a certain deity, whose surpassing brilliance and beauty illumined the entire Jeta Grove, late one night came to the presence of the Blessed One; having come to him and offered profound salutations he stood on one side and spoke to him reverently in the following verse:</p>\n<blockquote class='gatha'>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc2' href='#sc2'>SC 2</a>Many deities and human beings<br>\nHave pondered what are blessings,<br>\nWhich they hope will bring them safety:<br>\nDeclare to them, Sir, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><span class='add'>To this the Blessed One replied:</span></p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc3' href='#sc3'>SC 3</a>With fools no company keeping.<br>\nWith the wise ever consorting,<br>\nTo the worthy homage paying:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc4' href='#sc4'>SC 4</a>Congenial place to dwell,<br>\nIn the past merits making,<br>\nOne's self directed well:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc5' href='#sc5'>SC 5</a>Ample learning, in crafts ability,<br>\nWith a well-trained disciplining,<br>\nWell-spoken words, civility:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc6' href='#sc6'>SC 6</a>Mother, father well supporting,<br>\nWife and children duly cherishing,<br>\nTypes of work unconflicting:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc7' href='#sc7'>SC 7</a>Acts of giving, righteous living,<br>\nRelatives and kin supporting,<br>\nActions blameless then pursuing:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc8' href='#sc8'>SC 8</a>Avoiding evil and abstaining,<br>\nFrom besotting drinks refraining,<br>\nDiligence in Dhamma doing:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc9' href='#sc9'>SC 9</a>Right reverence and humility<br>\nContentment and a grateful bearing,<br>\nHearing Dhamma when it's timely:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc10' href='#sc10'>SC 10</a>Patience, meekness when corrected,<br>\nSeeing monks and then discussing<br>\nAbout the Dhamma when it's timely:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc11' href='#sc11'>SC 11</a>Self-restraint and holy life,<br>\nAll the Noble Truths in-seeing,<br>\nRealization of Nibbaana:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc12' href='#sc12'>SC 12</a>Though touched by worldly circumstances,<br>\nNever his mind is wavering,<br>\nSorrowless, stainless and secure:<br>\nThis, the Highest Blessing.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc13' href='#sc13'>SC 13</a>Since by acting in this way,<br>\nThey are everywhere unvanquished,<br>\nAnd everywhere they go in safety:<br>\nTheirs, the Highest Blessings.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<footer>\n<p>Translated by <span class='author'>Dr. R.L. Soni</span>.</p>\n<p>From <cite class='book' translate='no'>Life's Highest Blessings: The Maha Mangala Sutta</cite>, translated by Dr. R.L. Soni (Kandy: Buddhist Publication Society, <span class='publication-date'>1987</span></p>\n<p>This text was sourced from <a href='https://accesstoinsight.org/'>Access to Insight</a>. The original contained the following notice.</p>\n<p><strong>Terms of use:</strong> You may copy, reformat, reprint, republish, and redistribute this work in any medium whatsoever, provided that: (1) you only make such copies, etc. available free of charge and, in the case of reprinting, only in quantities of no more than 50 copies; (2) you clearly indicate that any derivatives of this work (including translations) are derived from this source document; and (3) you include the full text of this license in any copies or derivatives of this work. Otherwise, all rights reserved.</p>\n<p>Prepared for SuttaCentral by a volunteer.</p>\n</footer>\n</article>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}, "segmented": false, "suttaplex": {"acronym": "Snp 2.4", "alt_acronym": null, "volpages": "PTS Snp 46, PTS 47", "alt_volpages": null, "uid": "snp2.4", "blurb": "A list of the types of skillful behavior that give blessings and protection.", "difficulty": null, "original_title": "Maṅgalasutta", "root_lang": "pli", "root_lang_name": "Pāli", "type": "leaf", "from": null, "translated_title": "True Blessings ", "translations": [{"lang": "de", "lang_name": "Deutsch", "is_root": false, "author": "Sabbamitta", "author_short": "sabbamitta", "author_uid": "sabbamitta", "publication_date": "2019", "id": "snp2.4_translation-de-sabbamitta", "segmented": true, "title": "Segen ", "volpage": null, "has_comment": false}, {"lang": "en", "lang_name": "English", "is_root": false, "author": "Bhikk